    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The researchers developed a domain knowledge-enhanced theme expansion method that constrains large language models to act as semantic selectors rather than free-text generators during dataset retrieval. The system uses a three-tier 'domain-theme-instance' knowledge base to map user queries to actual metadata keywords, and was evaluated using a self-constructed geoscience dataset (GeoFinder) and an open-source benchmark (DataFinder) across both sparse and dense retrieval architectures.",
